# COM: End-to-end check of the coverage pipeline over an AMDGPU test-suite slice:
# COM:   a) baseline:       measure coverage of the existing suite slice (the baseline)
# COM:   b) candidate-test: measure coverage of an external test
# COM:   c) incremental:    report lines the new test covers that the baseline misses
# COM:   d) target-lines:   report which specific lines the baseline leaves uncovered
# COM:
# COM: Cross-check: the gaps incremental reports must match the lines target-lines flags, and a
# COM: baseline-covered line must show up in baseline output but not in incremental/target-lines.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/baseline %t/candidate_tests %t/incremental %t/target_lines
# RUN: %coverage baseline --output-dir %t/baseline --sancov %sancov --llvm-lit %llvm-lit --llc %sancov-llc --opt %sancov-opt --lit-filter CodeGen/AMDGPU/loop -j2
# RUN: %coverage candidate-test --output-dir %t/candidate_tests --llc %sancov-llc --candidate-tests-dir %S/fixtures/coverage-new-tests --n 1
# RUN: %coverage incremental --output-dir %t/incremental --sancov %sancov --line-coverage-uncovered-csv %t/baseline/line_coverage_uncovered.csv --llc-address-line-map-csv %t/baseline/llc_address_line_map.csv --candidate-tests-output-dir %t/candidate_tests
# RUN: %coverage target-lines --output-dir %t/target_lines --line-coverage-uncovered-csv %t/baseline/line_coverage_uncovered.csv --llvm-repo %llvm-repo --target-lines-csv %S/fixtures/target-lines-sample.csv

# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/line_coverage_summary.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/line_coverage_covered.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/line_coverage_partially.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/line_coverage_uncovered.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/llc_address_line_map.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/llc_line_point_summary.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/baseline/opt_line_point_summary.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/incremental/new_coverage.csv
# RUN: test -f %t/target_lines/target_lines_uncovered.csv

# COM: AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp:160 is covered by the test suite slice itself,
# COM: so it must appear in line_coverage_summary.csv as covered and must NOT be reported
# COM: as a new gain by incremental in new_coverage.csv.
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/baseline/line_coverage_summary.csv --check-prefix=BASELINE_CSV
# BASELINE_CSV: {{.*}}/AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp,160,covered

# COM: Per-status split CSVs must partition the combined summary (``file``, ``line`` only).
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/baseline/line_coverage_covered.csv --check-prefix=COVERED_CSV
# COVERED_CSV: {{.*}}/AMDGPUAlwaysInlinePass.cpp,160

# COM: These lines are uncovered by the test suite slice (uncovered in line_coverage_summary.csv)
# COM: but covered by the external test — manually confirmed with llvmorg-22.1.8 (RelWithDebInfo sancov build).
# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/baseline/line_coverage_summary.csv --check-prefix=SUMMARY_NONE
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,211,uncovered
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,222,uncovered
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUAsmPrinter.cpp,581,uncovered
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,590,uncovered
# SUMMARY_NONE-DAG: {{.*}}AMDGPUHSAMetadataStreamer.cpp,680,uncovered

# RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file=%t/baseline/line_coverage_uncovered.csv --check-prefix=UNCOVERED_CSV
